# Paperspace ComfyUI Troubleshooting

## Rule 1: Custom Node Problems — Update First, Then Reinstall Requirements

When a custom node fails to load or a node type is missing, the **first action** is always:

1. `git -C /storage/stable-diffusion-comfy/custom_nodes/<node-dir> pull` — update the node to latest
2. Reinstall its requirements into the venv:
   ```bash
   source /tmp/sd_comfy-env/bin/activate
   pip install -r /storage/stable-diffusion-comfy/custom_nodes/<node-dir>/requirements.txt
   ```
3. Then restart ComfyUI and check logs again before doing anything else.

Only dig deeper (missing packages, version conflicts, patching) if the node still fails after update + reinstall.
